WEBVTT

00:04.462 --> 00:05.964
[intriguing music playing]

00:08.508 --> 00:10.427
[frantic electronic music playing]

00:22.897 --> 00:24.274
[lyrics in Japanese]

01:34.427 --> 01:35.970
[music fades]

01:36.054 --> 01:37.931
THE BEGINNING

01:38.014 --> 01:39.224
COCKATIELS ARE RICH

01:39.307 --> 01:41.601
[straining grunts]

01:45.563 --> 01:46.940
[Tetsujo] Okay, this is the place.

01:47.816 --> 01:49.442
[Ton] Whoa, it's huge!

01:49.526 --> 01:52.946
[Ushishimada] So,
this is the landlord's mansion, eh?

01:53.530 --> 01:55.198
All right, here's the plan.

01:55.281 --> 01:58.451
We have to make it look like
she died naturally in her own home.

01:59.035 --> 02:01.621
Because if En finds out
she died at our place,

02:01.704 --> 02:04.207
then things are gonna get
real messy indeed.

02:05.792 --> 02:07.710
Hey, Saji. What are you doing?

02:07.794 --> 02:10.797
Our embroidery side hustle.
The deadline's today.

02:13.800 --> 02:14.843
[Ton gasps]

02:14.926 --> 02:17.220
She actually had
security cameras installed!

02:17.303 --> 02:19.973
Ugh, rich people. They're gross!

02:20.890 --> 02:23.476
Hey, guys, look over there.

02:26.479 --> 02:28.356
That's the main security unit.

02:28.439 --> 02:30.191
If we can somehow disable it,

02:30.275 --> 02:32.610
then the security cameras
should stop working.

02:33.111 --> 02:34.988
- Ton.
- Huh? Mm.

02:41.536 --> 02:46.249
Distance to target looks like
it'll be around 35 meters. Okay...

02:48.042 --> 02:49.002
Got it.

02:49.085 --> 02:50.503
[electronic beeping]

02:50.587 --> 02:51.504
[whirring]

03:01.055 --> 03:02.473
[beep]

03:02.557 --> 03:04.225
[powering down whirring]

03:04.309 --> 03:05.977
[Ushishimada] Amazing! Ha!

03:06.060 --> 03:08.354
What a awesome shot, you crazy pig!

03:08.438 --> 03:09.981
[both chuckling]

03:10.064 --> 03:12.483
- [all] Let's go!
- [suspenseful music playing]

03:12.567 --> 03:14.694
[automated voice] To unlock,
please insert smoke.

03:14.777 --> 03:16.571
To unlock, please insert smoke.

03:16.654 --> 03:18.489
The front door has a smoke lock...

03:18.573 --> 03:21.743
The door won't open unless we have
some of the landlord's smoke.

03:21.826 --> 03:23.661
What do you think we should do?

03:23.745 --> 03:26.122
We can't waste any more time
hanging around outside...

03:26.206 --> 03:27.248
[Ushishimada] Okay!

03:27.332 --> 03:29.500
Looks like this is where I come in!

03:29.584 --> 03:31.002
[strained grunting]

03:31.085 --> 03:32.754
[strained groaning]

03:34.964 --> 03:36.132
[bars creaking]

03:37.091 --> 03:39.260
[strained groaning continues]

03:46.351 --> 03:48.144
[strained yelling]

03:48.228 --> 03:50.146
[laughing triumphantly]

03:50.230 --> 03:52.315
How'd ya like my super strength!?

03:52.398 --> 03:53.900
- [chuckling]
- [all] Wow!

03:53.983 --> 03:57.278
Whatever, let's hurry up and get inside.

03:57.362 --> 03:59.822
It's so dark out here
I can't see my embroidery.

03:59.906 --> 04:02.784
[Ushishimada] Seriously?
Why the hell did you come here?

04:02.867 --> 04:04.369
[Ton] So... heavy...

04:05.078 --> 04:07.664
She must weigh about 400 kilos!

04:07.747 --> 04:10.541
So much space. This is just the hall?

04:10.625 --> 04:13.169
Well, let's steal something
when we leave here.

04:13.670 --> 04:15.421
Toilet paper would be good.

04:15.505 --> 04:16.923
[Ushishimada] Ugh.

04:17.006 --> 04:20.885
Seeing something like this,
I can't help but feel a little guilty.

04:20.969 --> 04:22.220
Let's just hurry up.

04:22.303 --> 04:24.931
This death needs to look
as natural as possible.

04:27.141 --> 04:29.769
When you think about most
of the accidents that happen at home,

04:29.852 --> 04:32.188
accidentally drowning
in the bath tub is one of them.

04:34.357 --> 04:35.191
Huh?

04:36.317 --> 04:38.194
The temperature's just right!

04:38.278 --> 04:41.781
[Tetsujo] Hang on. Almost there. Damn it.

04:41.864 --> 04:43.157
[grunting]

04:43.241 --> 04:44.284
Oh, I did it!

04:45.285 --> 04:46.411
Ergh!

04:46.494 --> 04:49.414
- [Ton] Heave!
- [all straining]

04:49.497 --> 04:50.707
[all gasping]

04:54.836 --> 04:56.254
[Saji] Very natural.

05:01.134 --> 05:03.052
If we wrap the rope around her like this,

05:03.136 --> 05:05.805
we can make it look like
she chose to end her life.

05:06.848 --> 05:08.558
[Tetsujo] Dokuga, you write it?

05:08.641 --> 05:09.684
Yeah.

05:12.061 --> 05:13.104
It's natural, right?

05:13.187 --> 05:14.522
I CAN'T KEEP LIVING ANYMORE

05:14.605 --> 05:17.025
Hey! Coming down!

05:17.108 --> 05:18.651
Yeah, go ahead.

05:18.735 --> 05:19.819
[Ton] Ready, and...

05:19.902 --> 05:23.823
By the way, Dokuga,
who was the person you saw killing Risu?

05:24.324 --> 05:25.783
Was it someone we already know?

05:26.701 --> 05:27.535
[Dokuga sighs]

05:27.618 --> 05:30.121
- That's it, come on.
- [straining]

05:30.204 --> 05:35.251
Also, you not being able to kill Risu...
Is that really true?

05:36.044 --> 05:37.503
Yeah. It's all true.

05:37.587 --> 05:40.381
Are you kidding?
There's no way you wouldn't be able to.

05:40.465 --> 05:42.383
[both straining]

05:47.638 --> 05:48.556
That's the thing.

05:49.390 --> 05:50.516
[gasps]

05:50.600 --> 05:53.561
The issue Is to do with Risu's Magic.

05:54.479 --> 05:56.939
Risu's... Magic?

05:57.023 --> 05:59.692
[both whimpering nervously]

05:59.776 --> 06:02.153
[Ton and Ushishimada] Dokuga!

06:03.196 --> 06:05.948
- [dramatic music playing]
- [strained grunting]

06:06.032 --> 06:07.200
Dokuga!

06:08.659 --> 06:11.037
[Dokuga straining]

06:14.332 --> 06:16.501
[screeching]

06:16.584 --> 06:19.003
- [all screaming]
- What the hell is that?!

06:19.670 --> 06:22.382
[creature hissing, snarling]

06:23.383 --> 06:24.634
Dokuga!

06:26.135 --> 06:27.512
[music fades]

06:29.764 --> 06:33.768
[Ton] Oh, I know what this thing is.
It's a diet insect!

06:33.851 --> 06:37.605
If you keep one of those in your stomach,
then it absorbs whatever you eat!

06:37.688 --> 06:40.775
So it came out after she died? Ah well.

06:41.359 --> 06:43.194
This all looks pretty natural to me.

06:43.277 --> 06:44.654
[Ushishimada] Which part?

06:44.737 --> 06:45.696
[Tetsujo] Dokuga!

06:45.780 --> 06:48.449
- Let's just take what we can and leave!
- [Tetsujo] I got you, come on!

06:48.533 --> 06:51.035
Look, I've finally finished my embroidery.

06:51.619 --> 06:54.997
I just hope it will end up becoming
some lovely lady's handkerchief.

06:55.081 --> 06:56.833
[Ushishimada] Come on, let's go!

06:57.708 --> 07:00.044
[Nikaido] Wow! What wonderful embroidery!

07:00.128 --> 07:04.674
It's really nice that girls get
to enjoy such lovely underwear.

07:06.759 --> 07:07.635
[distant wailing]

07:07.718 --> 07:09.387
[Chidaruma] Near the entrance of hell,

07:09.470 --> 07:12.932
there lies a small store
that remains nameless.

07:13.015 --> 07:14.434
CUTE BUTCHER

07:20.690 --> 07:23.192
[man] Whoa, no way.
What kind of store is this?

07:23.276 --> 07:25.445
[devil] Uh, one that sells meat.

07:25.528 --> 07:27.947
[man] But I don't see
a shopkeeper anywhere.

07:28.030 --> 07:30.783
[devil] That's because
you're still a devil trainee.

07:30.867 --> 07:32.285
You can't see him yet.

07:32.368 --> 07:34.328
Look, you can see his shadow, right?

07:35.329 --> 07:37.832
He's neither a devil nor a Sorcerer.

07:37.915 --> 07:40.209
He's neither good nor evil.

07:40.918 --> 07:42.378
[uneasy music playing]

07:43.754 --> 07:45.381
I'll take some meat.

07:45.465 --> 07:47.091
[butcher chattering]

07:49.427 --> 07:51.345
[trainee] So what is this meat, then?

07:51.429 --> 07:52.555
[devil chuckles]

07:52.638 --> 07:54.557
It's the meat of a certain creature.

07:54.640 --> 07:58.352
Once you eat it,
your body will start turning into a devil.

07:58.436 --> 08:00.354
- [phone ringing]
- [butcher chattering]

08:01.689 --> 08:03.357
[ringing continues]

08:06.068 --> 08:08.112
[Chidaruma] Thanks, I'm counting on you.

08:09.697 --> 08:15.077
Asu, you kept a secret from us.
From your own comrades.

08:15.578 --> 08:18.247
That's something I cannot forgive.

08:19.373 --> 08:21.584
I just made a call to Store.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.837
You know what that means, don't you, Asu?

08:24.921 --> 08:26.380
[ominous music playing]

08:35.431 --> 08:37.850
[excited snarling]

08:37.934 --> 08:40.353
[screeching]

08:42.647 --> 08:45.608
You are no longer fit to be a devil, Asu.

08:45.691 --> 08:47.610
- [grunts]
- [pained groaning]

08:47.693 --> 08:50.613
- [humming cheerfully]
- [pained groaning]

08:54.909 --> 08:56.619
[chuckling]

08:57.411 --> 08:58.871
[humming cheerfully]

08:59.664 --> 09:00.873
[chuckles]

09:00.957 --> 09:01.999
[humming]

09:04.085 --> 09:05.086
[Chidaruma strains]

09:10.007 --> 09:12.927
Store, you're up. He's all yours.

09:14.011 --> 09:16.347
[butcher chattering creepily]

09:23.437 --> 09:25.856
[chattering]

09:33.447 --> 09:35.533
[screechy squawk, chattering]

09:41.998 --> 09:44.000
[butcher moaning]

09:49.505 --> 09:52.341
Here, Store, that's for you.

09:52.425 --> 09:53.426
[butcher] Oh!

09:53.509 --> 09:55.428
- [butcher gnawing]
- [Asu whimpering]

09:56.053 --> 09:58.681
Asu, you are such a fool.

09:58.764 --> 09:59.932
[Asu grunts, groans]

10:00.516 --> 10:05.313
No. You're no longer Asu.
Kawajiri the Sorcerer, wasn't it?

10:07.398 --> 10:09.317
Farewell, Kawajiri.

10:09.400 --> 10:12.361
You can go back
to living as a Sorcerer now.

10:15.406 --> 10:16.574
[Kawajiri whimpering]

10:17.158 --> 10:21.162
My power.
I can feel it fading away from me...

10:21.912 --> 10:23.831
Nikaido...

10:28.419 --> 10:29.670
EAST ZAGAN TORQUE

10:29.754 --> 10:31.088
[vendor] Come and get 'em!

10:31.172 --> 10:33.591
Anybody want some freshly baked bread?

10:33.674 --> 10:36.927
They're filled with lots of cheese,
lots of stew, and a whole lotta cream.

10:37.011 --> 10:39.221
- I'll take three, please!
- Coming up!

10:39.305 --> 10:40.598
[jaunty music playing]

10:43.934 --> 10:47.063
Wow you really are eating that
with your mask on, aren't you?

10:47.146 --> 10:50.983
So I'm the one paying for these?
Okay, that's fine. They're on me!

10:53.110 --> 10:54.862
- Mm.
- [chuckling excitedly]

10:54.945 --> 10:57.239
- Yum!
- Aah, cheesy!

10:57.323 --> 10:58.491
[chuckles]

10:58.574 --> 11:00.242
- [Caiman slurping]
- Hmm?

11:00.326 --> 11:02.203
[Caiman slurping] Mm!

11:05.831 --> 11:07.333
[vendor] Come and get 'em.

11:07.416 --> 11:10.753
Freshly baked bread with stew,
cheese, and cream...

11:10.836 --> 11:13.255
[butcher chattering happily]

11:13.339 --> 11:16.258
NEW MEAT SHIPMENT ARRIVED!

11:20.304 --> 11:23.808
[Chidaruma] The evening before
I turned Asu back from a devil

11:23.891 --> 11:25.518
to just a sorcerer.

11:26.352 --> 11:27.311
[Nikaido sighs]

11:27.395 --> 11:30.356
I feel so much more at ease
with my own mask on.

11:30.439 --> 11:32.900
[gasps] Oh, this is bad.
The evening just flew by!

11:32.983 --> 11:34.944
I really should go to bed.

11:35.486 --> 11:37.113
But first things first.

11:37.196 --> 11:39.448
I need to find a good hiding place
for my mask

11:39.532 --> 11:41.158
so I can keep it safe and sound.

11:41.242 --> 11:44.662
Nope, there's no way I'm hiding it
down here. It'll certainly be found.

11:45.287 --> 11:48.165
Oh, maybe somewhere in here? Hmm?

11:50.751 --> 11:54.672
What's this? A notebook?
Could it belong to Nikaido?

11:55.548 --> 11:57.258
I see it has a smoke lock.

11:57.341 --> 11:58.592
[giggles]

11:58.676 --> 11:59.969
No problem!

12:00.678 --> 12:03.639
A lock like this is nothing
against my Magic!

12:08.269 --> 12:10.688
MY HEART'S DIARY

12:11.397 --> 12:13.023
"My heart's diary..."

12:13.107 --> 12:14.191
[giggling]

12:14.275 --> 12:17.194
This girl has no taste whatsoever!

12:17.278 --> 12:18.738
All right, let's see...

12:18.821 --> 12:21.991
"I feel as though the power
of the devil's contract inside of me

12:22.074 --> 12:23.075
is crushing me"

12:23.159 --> 12:26.787
If this carries on,
I may disappear completely.

12:26.871 --> 12:28.414
But before that happens,

12:28.497 --> 12:31.083
I've decided I should write
about my Magic in this diary.

12:31.167 --> 12:32.877
[pained groaning]

12:32.960 --> 12:36.255
So that even when I'm completely
controlled by the contract,

12:36.338 --> 12:38.382
I will never use my Magic.

12:38.466 --> 12:40.259
DOOR TO THE PAST

12:43.137 --> 12:46.390
I grew up in a tiny village
deep in the mountains.

12:46.474 --> 12:50.060
Although my parents passed away
when I was only a baby,

12:50.686 --> 12:52.646
I was always a happy child.

12:53.147 --> 12:54.565
I had a kind auntie and uncle,

12:54.648 --> 12:57.359
and Kawajiri,
who always looked out for me,

12:57.443 --> 12:59.445
treated me like he was my big brother.

12:59.945 --> 13:01.572
Every day there was fun.

13:02.698 --> 13:06.160
That was until my best friend,
Yakumo, disappeared.

13:06.243 --> 13:08.704
[yawning] I can't go on! Too tired!

13:09.497 --> 13:11.415
I'll read the rest of it tomorrow.

13:11.999 --> 13:14.335
[whooshing]

13:14.418 --> 13:15.586
[En] All right, everyone

13:15.669 --> 13:17.379
I want to hear your opinion
on a new product

13:17.463 --> 13:19.340
I'm planning on selling under my brand.

13:19.423 --> 13:22.802
It's called the "En-shaped Mushroom Doll."

13:22.885 --> 13:25.846
It's an edible mushroom pet
made for my fans.

13:25.930 --> 13:27.681
It's awesome!

13:28.432 --> 13:31.560
They react to things
like humidity and airflow.

13:31.644 --> 13:34.897
So cute! I must have one!

13:35.523 --> 13:36.357
[yelps]

13:36.440 --> 13:38.692
Although they're prone
to becoming parasites,

13:38.776 --> 13:40.528
attaching themselves to living beings.

13:40.611 --> 13:41.654
I'll work on that.

13:42.196 --> 13:45.616
What do you think?
I'd like to hear your opinion, Nikaido.

13:45.699 --> 13:49.620
Well, let's see... Oh, I know!
It'd be great if they were bigger!

13:49.703 --> 13:51.831
Y'know, if they were the same size as you!

13:51.914 --> 13:54.583
Good opinion, Nikaido! Approved!

13:54.667 --> 13:55.751
Oh, yay!

13:55.835 --> 13:59.380
[Fujita] Stop it, please!
Someone take this thing off of me!

14:00.548 --> 14:02.216
By the way, Nikaido,

14:02.299 --> 14:04.510
do you still not feel like
using your Magic?

14:04.593 --> 14:07.054
- [gasps] I don't want to talk about it!
- [En] Ugh.

14:07.137 --> 14:11.308
Wait! Nikaido!
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to force you.

14:11.392 --> 14:12.977
Nikaido...

14:15.104 --> 14:17.314
Oh wow. That caught me off guard.

14:17.398 --> 14:20.234
Although pretending to be upset
and running away from him

14:20.317 --> 14:21.569
won't work much longer.

14:22.278 --> 14:24.029
I worked up quite a sweat.

14:24.113 --> 14:27.157
Maybe I should take a bath
and continue reading that diary.

14:29.910 --> 14:32.329
Ah, right...

14:32.413 --> 14:35.541
"It wasn't until I was around
two or three years old

14:35.624 --> 14:38.586
that I was first able
to properly use Magic."

14:40.421 --> 14:42.756
Wow, Nikaido, that's great!

14:42.840 --> 14:44.466
[mysterious music playing]

14:45.843 --> 14:47.011
[Nikaido] Huh?

14:47.094 --> 14:49.555
- What is this?
- A candy?

14:49.638 --> 14:52.766
Well, whatever it is,
I'm sure you'll figure it out eventually,

14:52.850 --> 14:54.268
once you make more smoke!

14:54.351 --> 14:56.312
Nikaido will practice!

14:56.395 --> 14:57.771
- [woman] Hey!
- Hmm?

14:57.855 --> 15:00.274
Kawajiri! Nikaido!

15:00.357 --> 15:02.026
- [Kawajiri] Yakumo!
- [giggles]

15:02.109 --> 15:05.487
[Nikaido] Yakumo's Magic gave her
the ability to fly!

15:06.822 --> 15:08.365
When she was a baby,

15:08.449 --> 15:11.744
she was found floating down the river
by sheer coincidence.

15:12.244 --> 15:14.204
Because of that, she always used to say

15:14.288 --> 15:16.457
that she had great luck wherever she went.

15:17.875 --> 15:21.295
She was always so cheerful
and wasn't afraid of anything.

15:21.879 --> 15:23.005
[Yakumo gasps]

15:24.757 --> 15:27.426
- Oh no, it's another dead child.
- I'm scared!

15:27.509 --> 15:30.262
That means
there must be some hunters nearby.

15:30.346 --> 15:32.181
We should leave here right now.

15:32.264 --> 15:36.936
[Nikaido] Hunters... they were people
who would kidnap Sorcerer children.

15:38.020 --> 15:42.066
Many children died because of fighting
between different groups of hunters.

15:42.650 --> 15:44.318
[man] Young man...

15:44.401 --> 15:48.322
Leave those kids here and go.
You see, one of mine just died.

15:48.405 --> 15:49.323
[Yakumo] A hunter!

15:49.406 --> 15:52.326
Asshole. I'll punch you!!

15:54.161 --> 15:55.079
Huh?

15:55.162 --> 15:56.246
[Yakumo straining]

15:58.040 --> 16:00.084
Huh? They vanished!

16:01.043 --> 16:02.836
[Nikaido] Kawajiri was a Sorcerer.

16:02.920 --> 16:05.756
His magic allowed him
to travel anywhere freely.

16:06.423 --> 16:08.175
He also had a kind of clairvoyance,

16:08.258 --> 16:10.719
which meant
he could choose his destination.

16:11.220 --> 16:13.347
- Hello, Auntie! We're back.
- [gasps]

16:13.430 --> 16:17.267
[uncle] Kawajiri, you really should stop
relying on magic all the time

16:17.351 --> 16:19.353
and try to walk a little once in a while.

16:19.436 --> 16:20.479
[auntie] He's right.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.856
We only just managed
to escape from a hunter.

16:22.940 --> 16:25.359
[Yakumo squeals]
We're eating gyozas today!

16:25.442 --> 16:28.320
[Nikaido] Gyozas were always
Auntie's specialty.

16:28.821 --> 16:31.156
I wonder what Gyozas are?

16:31.240 --> 16:35.744
I guess I'm really not too familiar with
the food of the commoners. Oh well.

16:36.328 --> 16:39.248
It was around the time
that I was four years old...

16:39.999 --> 16:41.125
Yah!

16:41.959 --> 16:43.627
What are you both doing?

16:43.711 --> 16:45.629
Welcome home, Kawajiri!

16:45.713 --> 16:48.048
I'm training Nikaido
so she knows how to fight!

16:48.132 --> 16:50.259
It's good. Now I know how to break boards.

16:50.342 --> 16:52.845
Yeah, but aren't you bleeding, though?

16:52.928 --> 16:54.513
This is too much, Yakumo.

16:54.596 --> 16:58.058
But this is the only way
her fists will ever get stronger.

16:58.142 --> 16:59.768
Hmm? What is that?

16:59.852 --> 17:02.771
Huh? Oh. This thing?

17:04.314 --> 17:07.609
I got it the other day from a devil
who gave me his business card.

17:08.110 --> 17:09.903
He made it especially for me.

17:10.404 --> 17:11.947
So cool!

17:12.656 --> 17:15.034
I've been given an invitation
to become a devil.

17:15.117 --> 17:17.453
Oh? Hmm.

17:18.954 --> 17:21.165
[Nikaido giggling playfully]

17:25.627 --> 17:28.047
[uncle] Make sure
you do your best, Kawajiri.

17:28.130 --> 17:31.300
[auntie] That armor's very impressive.
Will you be okay?

17:31.383 --> 17:34.511
[Kawajiri] Yeah, apparently,
living everyday life in this thing

17:34.595 --> 17:36.680
is the first phase of training.

17:37.514 --> 17:39.433
Well, I'm off to work.

17:40.642 --> 17:42.728
What's the point if he doesn't walk?

17:43.520 --> 17:47.316
[Nikaido] That day, I was in the house
on my own for the first time.

17:47.900 --> 17:52.404
As soon as I finished wrapping the gyoza,
I realized I had nothing else to do.

17:52.488 --> 17:53.822
[yawning]

17:55.324 --> 17:56.784
A thought then dawned.

17:56.867 --> 18:00.829
It had been a while since I used my Magic,
so I tried letting out some smoke.

18:04.416 --> 18:07.586
Maybe it was because I was a bit older,
my power had increased,

18:07.669 --> 18:10.756
but the cube was almost
the same size as me.

18:12.174 --> 18:14.551
It also now had buttons and levers on it.

18:15.052 --> 18:18.013
I tried pressing all the buttons
and pulling all the levers,

18:18.097 --> 18:19.723
but nothing seemed to work.

18:20.682 --> 18:23.519
I decided
that in order to master my Magic,

18:23.602 --> 18:25.479
I needed to start practicing.

18:26.438 --> 18:28.357
[static crackling]

18:29.608 --> 18:31.193
[Nikaido] What I didn't know

18:31.276 --> 18:34.363
was that would be the beginning
of a terrifying event...

18:34.446 --> 18:36.365
- [En] Nikaido!
- [mushroom pet] En!

18:36.448 --> 18:38.367
[En] It's me. Open up.

18:38.450 --> 18:41.620
I'm here to apologize.
I also brought you presents.

18:41.703 --> 18:44.373
[Chota] Just when
things were getting interesting.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.875
I really do need to dry my hair first...

18:46.959 --> 18:47.960
What?

18:50.712 --> 18:51.755
The hell?

18:51.839 --> 18:52.840
THE PLACE OF CONFORT BERITH

18:52.923 --> 18:54.591
[Nikaido] Seriously?! Now you're saying

18:54.675 --> 18:57.344
you don't know the location
of the Cross-Eyes hideout?!

18:57.845 --> 18:58.929
Well, no.

18:59.012 --> 19:01.723
- [Nikaido] Ugh!
- I just wanted to travel with you both.

19:01.807 --> 19:02.641
Sorry...

19:02.724 --> 19:05.978
But I'm sure we'll find it
if we look for it!

19:06.061 --> 19:07.813
How can we do that?

19:08.313 --> 19:10.399
We have absolutely no information.

19:10.482 --> 19:12.151
Also, it'll be getting dark soon.

19:12.234 --> 19:15.028
Right, well, let's find
somewhere to rest for the night!

19:15.112 --> 19:17.656
Then we can start our search
tomorrow morning!

19:17.739 --> 19:18.949
[Nikaido] Hmm.

19:19.575 --> 19:21.410
What do you think, Caiman?

19:22.327 --> 19:23.287
[Caiman] Huh?

19:24.079 --> 19:25.831
Uh, yeah...

19:27.457 --> 19:28.584
Caiman...

19:30.002 --> 19:34.381
But will there even be a place
to stay in such a small village?

19:34.464 --> 19:35.674
Yeah, you're right.

19:35.757 --> 19:38.427
- Oh, how about this place?
- [Nikaido] Hmm?

19:39.052 --> 19:40.679
BERITH HOT SPRINGS

19:40.762 --> 19:43.182
[all] Welcome, one and all!

19:43.265 --> 19:46.685
[leader] It looks like
three guests have arrived.

19:46.768 --> 19:48.061
Oh...

19:48.770 --> 19:51.398
A married couple and their child.

19:51.481 --> 19:52.816
- [Nikaido chuckles awkwardly]
- Huh?

19:52.900 --> 19:54.818
MAGMA BATH

19:54.902 --> 19:57.821
- [En] Nikaido, please open the door!
- [Chota] Oh no...

19:57.905 --> 20:00.199
- [En] Nikaido!
- What should I do? I'm back to me again!

20:00.282 --> 20:02.117
[whimpers, screams]

20:02.743 --> 20:05.329
Ouch! Huh?

20:05.412 --> 20:07.873
[En] What happened, Nikaido? Are you okay?

20:07.956 --> 20:12.085
[Chota] Isn't this the contract from En
that was inside Nikaido's body?

20:12.878 --> 20:14.254
[door creaking]

20:16.006 --> 20:17.174
Nikaido!

20:18.425 --> 20:21.094
Nikaido, I'm sorry about earlier

20:21.178 --> 20:24.640
- I--
- I forgive you, honey.

20:24.723 --> 20:26.725
- But--
- Chota, you stupid bird!

20:26.808 --> 20:28.727
What the hell
do you think you're doing here?

20:28.810 --> 20:30.812
[Chota] I can explain everything!

20:31.730 --> 20:32.606
[En] What?!

20:33.273 --> 20:36.360
Nikaido actually ran away
with that lizard man?

20:36.443 --> 20:38.612
So that means the Nikaido that was here...

20:38.695 --> 20:40.614
Heh, surprise! That was me--

20:40.697 --> 20:42.866
- Turn to mushroom!
- [Chota screams]

20:42.950 --> 20:45.702
- I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
- [En gasps]

20:45.786 --> 20:47.829
[pained gasping]

20:51.458 --> 20:53.961
Huh? It's so busy all of a sudden.

20:54.461 --> 20:57.547
Ah well,
I wonder where Ebisu's gone off to?

20:57.631 --> 20:58.882
She skipped work,

20:58.966 --> 21:02.052
even though we got our salary today
from the Big Boss.

21:02.135 --> 21:03.512
Not that it's much.

21:05.222 --> 21:08.100
I guess she isn't an official
member of the family anyway,

21:08.183 --> 21:09.893
so it doesn't really matter.

21:09.977 --> 21:12.312
She just stuck around for no reason.

21:12.396 --> 21:15.399
In fact, now might be
a good time to kick her out! Oh?

21:16.108 --> 21:17.401
Ebisu?

21:19.486 --> 21:21.530
I wonder where she's going?

21:21.613 --> 21:23.407
And with all that luggage...

21:24.533 --> 21:27.160
No way. Is she leaving?

21:29.037 --> 21:33.166
[scoffs] Fine, then.
Go if you want. I don't give a damn.

21:34.793 --> 21:36.253
Ebisu!

21:36.920 --> 21:38.588
[panting]

21:39.298 --> 21:41.341
[fatigued sigh, panting]

21:43.385 --> 21:45.387
Hey, where you going?

21:45.929 --> 21:47.180
[Ebisu] I'm going home.

21:47.264 --> 21:51.560
Wait, what? So does that mean...
Did you get your memories back?

21:53.228 --> 21:55.314
[Ebisu] Bye-bye, Fujita.

22:02.946 --> 22:04.448
[Japanese theme song playing]

23:30.659 --> 23:31.910
THE END

23:31.993 --> 23:34.079
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 16.

23:34.162 --> 23:36.498
Store sells a certain creature's meat.

23:36.581 --> 23:38.166
Natsuki is the one who pays.

23:38.250 --> 23:39.960
En found out many things.

23:40.043 --> 23:44.005
What we're going to learn in Episode 17.
it's still... lost in chaos.

23:44.089 --> 23:46.925
This is... Dorohedoro!
